WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.088
In the year 280, Emperor Wu of Jin, Sima Yan, decided to send his army to defeat Wu and reunite China.

00:00:08.438 --> 00:00:13.118
In the court, every general was full of energy and confidence.

00:00:13.468 --> 00:00:20.548
The Wu emperor Sun Hao spent all his days in pleasure, paying no attention at all to state affairs.

00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:28.986
The Jin forces advanced by land and water in a mighty sweep, heading straight for Jianye, the Wu capital.

00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:34.640
The fleet swept downstream with astonishing momentum — nothing could stop it.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:40.414
Sun Hao knew he could not defeat the Jin army, so he had no choice but to leave the city and surrender.

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:47.028
The three powers of Cao Wei, Shu Han, and Eastern Wu all finally came under the Jin dynasty.

00:00:47.378 --> 00:00:51.506
After so many years apart, the land was finally made one again.

00:00:51.856 --> 00:00:58.336
China was reunified, and the Three Kingdoms era, lasting nearly a hundred years, formally came to an end.

00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:02.982
The people hoped that from now on they could live peaceful, settled lives.

